{"id": "lg_elec-2026-09-14-005", "date": "2026-09-14", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 38, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": ["lg_elec"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": [], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.25, "keywords": ["record", "[否定]expand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "LG sells 15 US image patents to Honor as IP monetization expands", "content": "LG Electronics has transferred 15 US image-related standard essential patents to Honor in late August 2026, according to South Korean media reports citing US Patent and Trademark Office records. The deal extends LG's strategy of monetizing communications and video technology assets following its exit from the smartphone market in 2021.", "sources": [{"name": "digitimes_display", "url": "https://www.digitimes.com/news/a20260914PD243/lg-lg-electronics-honor-patent-technology.html", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-14-006", "date": "2026-09-14", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 38, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "AI demand lifts UMC, VIS, PSMC revenue", "content": "<p class=\"P1\" data-start=\"3849\" data-end=\"4197\">After mature-node price competition from 2023 to 2025, AI demand has spread from GPUs and HBM to power management ICs (PMICs), power components, networking chips and specialty processes. At the same time, aggressive price cutting by mature-node players in China has eased, pushing quotes for Taiwan foundries broadly higher since the start of 2026.", "sources": [{"name": "digitimes_display", "url": "https://www.digitimes.com/news/a20260914PD235/demand-revenue-price-umc-psmc.html", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "samsung_elec-2026-09-14-007", "date": "2026-09-14", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 38, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": ["samsung_elec"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": [], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Samsung, SK Hynix reject US$19 billion power prepayment as Korea speeds chip expansion", "content": "<p class=\"P1\" data-start=\"2838\" data-end=\"3117\">Samsung Electronics and SK Hynix have rejected a proposal to prepay KRW25 trillion (approx. US$18.7 billion) in electricity bills, highlighting the financing challenge facing South Korea as it accelerates semiconductor expansion and the power infrastructure needed to support it.", "sources": [{"name": "digitimes_display", "url": "https://www.digitimes.com/news/a20260914VL218/samsung-sk-hynix-expansion-electricity-infrastructure.html", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-14-008", "date": "2026-09-14", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 38, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "Taiwan eases investment rules for AI center infrastructure projects", "content": "Taiwan's government has limited budgets to build the AI computing infrastructure the country needs, and infrastructure that a government runs itself cannot easily turn a profit. To get around that constraint, the Ministry of Digital Affairs (MODA) introduced the AI computing center BOO (build-operate-own) public-private partnership project in April 2026, aiming to let private companies build and operate the infrastructure while tax incentives make the investment attractive to them.", "sources": [{"name": "digitimes_display", "url": "https://www.digitimes.com/news/a20260914PD209/infrastructure-investment-moda-taiwan-government.html", "type": "rss"}]}
